    "name": "Deposit Account Entity - EIS",
    "description": "This API retrieves, creates and/or maintains account data as well as transaction data in FIS for a deposit account. This collection of APIs allows retrieve, create, and validate capabilities for deposit account entity. Additionally, deposit account control attributes  can be retrieved to support the pre-validation of attributes prior to creating or maintaining the deposit account entity.\n## Service Domain Role:\nThe Deposit Account (which includes the Current Account or Demand Deposit Account, Savings Account, and Term Account) is a financial facility that represents the general checking account facility, savings account, or term account at the core of the consumer and small business banking activity. There is a range of supporting features that make up the standard facility (checks/cheques, standing orders, debit cards, phone and on-line banking services etc.). The fulfillment can include a range of optional services, fees and interest payments and penalties and will often be bundled and or underlie/support other financial facilities and financial transactions.\n## Examples of Use:\nA customer processes a series of services (e.g., request printed statements, initiate a transfer, set up a standing order) through the call center by accessing their current account. \nA consumer customer establishes a term deposit in order to  obtain a higher interest rate for excess funds they do not anticipate needing over the term of the deposit.\n\nContact Support:\n Name: EIS\n Email: EISSupportTeam@seacoastbank.com",
